---
title: Privacy Policy
description: Learn how SEDS Sri Lanka respects, handles, and protects your personal information and student privacy.
---

### 1. Overview & Commitment

Students for the Exploration and Development of Space Sri Lanka (SEDS Sri Lanka, "we", "our") respects your privacy. We are committed to protecting the personal information of our members, event attendees, donors, and website visitors.

This Privacy Policy outlines the information we collect, how it is used, and how your privacy is safeguarded across our official domain **[sedssl.org](https://sedssl.org)** and community platforms.

---

### 2. Information We Collect

We only collect information necessary to facilitate membership, organize educational events, and process merchandise orders:

- **Membership Applications**: Full name, email address, contact phone number, university or school affiliation, preferred chapter, and statement of interest when applying through our Join Us form.
- **Contact Inquiries**: Name, email address, topic/reason, and inquiry message submitted via our contact portal.
- **Event & Hackathon Registrations**: Participant details, team members, academic qualifications, and emergency contacts for in-person workshops and camps (e.g. International Observe the Moon Night).
- **Merchandise Orders**: Name, shipping address, contact number, and payment receipt confirmations submitted via our verified Tally order workflows.
- **Technical & Security Data**: Cloudflare Turnstile token validation and non-identifiable browser telemetry used solely to defend against automated spam and denial-of-service threats.

---

### 3. How We Use Your Information

The information collected is used exclusively for non-profit student space community operations:

1. **Membership Management**: Connecting applicants with their respective university chapters (e.g., SEDS Mora, SEDS Pera, SEDS Colombo) and technical divisions.
2. **Community Communications**: Sending transactional receipts, membership confirmations, workshop reminders, rocket launch updates, and newsletter notifications.
3. **Order Fulfillment**: Coordinating shipping and delivery of merchandise orders with local courier partners.
4. **Safety & Compliance**: Ensuring verified student identities during on-site rocketry and laboratory workshops.

We **never sell, rent, lease, or monetize** your personal information to third-party commercial advertisers or data brokers under any circumstances.

---

### 4. Data Security & Retention

- All web traffic and form submissions are transmitted over modern TLS/SSL encryption.
- Transactional emails are securely dispatched via the Resend API with no external database footprint.
- Membership records are accessible only by authorized members of the national Executive Committee and relevant Chapter Leads.

---

### 5. Media & Event Photography

During in-person space events, astronomy camps, and campus workshops, our media team may capture photos and video highlights for educational and promotional recaps. If you prefer not to appear in published media, simply inform the event coordinator on-site or contact our media team.

---

### 6. Your Rights & Inquiries

You have the right to request a summary of the personal data we hold about you, request corrections, or request complete removal from our membership directory at any time.

For any questions or privacy inquiries:

- **Email**: [contact@sedssl.org](mailto:contact@sedssl.org)
- **Official Domain**: [sedssl.org](https://sedssl.org)
